{title: Double Portion}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 2:1–15}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]From Gilgal we walked side by side
[Cm]Elijah said stay here, [Abmaj7]I must go
[Eb]But I swore I would not leave his side
As sure[Cm]ly as the Lord lives, no [Abmaj7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Give me a [Eb]double portion of your spirit
Before you are [Cm]taken from my sight
If I [Abmaj7]see you go, it shall be given
If not, [Bb]then let me be in the night [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
At Bethel the prophets asked me then [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm]Do you know he is being [Abmaj7]taken away?
[Eb]I said yes, I know, be still, my friend [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm]And we kept walking through the day [Abmaj7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Give me a [Eb]double portion of your spirit
Be[Ebmaj7/D]fore you are [Cm]taken from my sight
If I [Abmaj7]see you go, it shall be given
If not, [Bb]then let me be in the night [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
At the Jordan river bank we stood
[Cm]Fifty prophets watched us [Abmaj7]from afar
[Eb]He rolled up his cloak, striking the flood
[Cm]The water parted on the dry [Abmaj7]ground star
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
A chariot of fire split the sky [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm]Horses of flame and a [Abmaj7]whirlwind sound
[Eb]Elijah rose up, I cried and I sighed
[Ebmaj7/D]My fa[Cm]ther, the chariots of this [Abmaj7]ground
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]I took his cloak and struck the water [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm]The Jordan split to the [Abmaj7]right and left
[Eb]The spirit of Elijah is the answer
[Ebmaj7/D]The [Cm]God of Elijah is what I [Abmaj7]sought
{end_of_verse}
